hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1738","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil who said: Aqil ibn Abi Talib married and came out to us, and we said: With harmony and sons. He said: Enough, do not say that, for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us from that, and said: Say: May Allah bless her for you and bless you for her."
"1739","Ismail, and he is Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan that Aqil ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, married a woman from Banu Jusham, and the people came to him and said: With harmony and sons. He said: Do not do that. They said: What shall we say, O Abu Yazid? He said: Say: May Allah bless you and bless upon you; thus we were commanded."
